0..77 Comment "// A short string keeps its bytes inside itself and a long one in a buffer on"
78..149 Comment "// the heap: a string of at most 23 bytes, its zero making 24, needs no"
150..228 Comment "// allocation, and a copy of it is a copy of those bytes. Where the bytes live"
229..299 Comment "// is not observable: a string reads as the same bytes either way (the"
300..369 Comment "// small-string optimisation of libc++\'s `std::string`, and of Rust\'s"
370..417 Comment "// `compact_str`, which keeps 24 bytes inline)."
419..465 Comment "// The lists; the byte lists; the owned bytes."
